  - POLICY NOTE: this is NOT an instance of the standing "oral history yields to documented facts" directive. No document was overridden. Oral history supplied context that made four documented records mutually consistent. Recorded explicitly in the conflict's resolution field so the distinction isn't lost.
  - WHY THE TWO AWARDS DIVERGE -- worth stating because it looked like an error and isn't: the L&V Games could be abstracted into individual and online challenges, so the competition survived; the Order of Owens recognises canoe-tripping leadership, which cannot be earned without a canoe, a trip, or a camp to do it at, so it lapsed. The two honours measure different things and their records diverge accordingly (f_2009, inferred).
  - CORRECTED THE STANDING INFERENCE: lv-games.md's body had said the single skipped season was "most likely the COVID-cancelled 2020 season." That was wrong about WHICH season -- it was 2021. Corrected in place with an explicit note that the earlier reading predated the trophy transcription, rather than silently rewritten.
